      "content": "I hear how profoundly the idea of your souls being together can make his absence feel like a catastrophic mistake rather than a simply sad event. While grief does not necessarily \"get better\" in a way that instantly returns to the old you, it often involves a painful but necessary process of rewriting your personal narrative to include a life chapter dedicated to loving him. you are not pretending to be alive, because your feelings are undeniably real evidence of a deep, meaningful connection that shaped who you became.",
